 ## Background
-Hybrid-memory compositing was analyzed in the context of large-scale volume rendering on multi-core and many-core systems. The approach builds on observations by Peterka et al. that reducing the number of compositors at higher concurrencies increases overall performance [S1]. The specific implementation details and performance metrics (6x fewer messages, 2.2x total speedup at 216,000 cores) are derived from studies on systems like JaguarPF and Longhorn [S1].
